  copy imports. Fixed at every measured site: the watchdog lane-c scratch now mirrors the
  sibling adapter src; scripts/repin-vendor.mjs, check-citations' T-82 arm and the four
  self-fix suites stage scripts/lib/ (the last four through a new shared helper,
  self-fix-tests/scratch-scripts.mjs).

TEST ROUND
  Unit/type: typecheck PASS; bun test 1244 pass / 3 skip / 1 fail — the SAME single
             environmental failure as the recorded pre-change baseline
             (`REAL toolchain probe: ast-grep passes, the deprecated sg wrapper fails`).
  Gates    : verify:gates 5/5 PASS; test:qa PASS; verify-dist-fresh 23/23 FRESH (double
             rebuild, byte-identical); verify-pack-closure PASS; verify-docs-parity PASS
             (41 pairs, 0 dead links); verify-manual-paths PASS;
             check-citations 25/25 (was 21/25).
  User-facing: node scripts/run-qa-lanes.mjs (26 real-boot lanes + 6 gates) run twice —
             once on a pristine `git archive` of HEAD and once on the refactored tree.
             28 verdicts identical; 2 explained by the gitignored packed artifact's
             presence (relocate-smoke, skill-catalog-probe — packing the PRISTINE tree
             reproduces the after result); 2 re-run to PASS on both trees
             (session-start-team under a longer cap, workmate-library after its own retry).
             No lane regressed.

  ENVIRONMENT FACT that decides whether a lane tests anything at all, now documented:
    BUN_TMPDIR must point INSIDE the workspace. BUN_INSTALL (~/.bun) is read-only under
    the file sandbox, so a bun-spawning lane dies with
    `EROFS accessing temporary directory` a few milliseconds in — a FAIL that never
    reached an assertion.

